{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:09:51.548Z","ordinal":19122,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a0081e-313c-7df0-b3e1-da61a5b22476","author":"/root/verifier","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/verifier\nPayload:\nVerifier report: all executable gates passed, but I found four actionable coverage gaps.\n\nFindings:\n\n1. `PaymentRefundService`’s advisory lock has no concurrency test or mutant. Deleting `pg_advisory_xact_lock` at `lib/paymentRefundService.ts:21` could allow simultaneous retries to create/submit duplicate refund attempts without any current test failing.\n\n2. The refund-to-cancellation integrity guard at `lib/paymentRefundService.ts:30`–`36` is untested. There is no assertion for a non-cancellation, wrong amount, wrong PaymentIntent, or wrong currency reaching the service; deleting the entire guard is outside the supplied mutant selection.\n\n3. Migration coverage omits three important database mechanisms:\n   - `PaymentRefundAttempt_providerRefundId_key`\n   - `PaymentRefund_bookingStatusChangeId_fkey`\n   - `PaymentRefundAttempt_paymentRefundId_fkey`\n\n   My native scratch proof confirmed all three currently work, but no automated test or reported mutant would catch their future removal.\n\n4. `retryBookingRefundAction` tests cover owner success and cross-user denial only. They do not constrain its no-refund validation result or the fail-safe mapping of a provider/service exception to the stable `payment.refund` error. The refund status mapper also lacks focused cases for `requires_action`, `canceled`, and a missing Stripe refund status.\n\nExecutable results:\n\n- Prisma generate: passed with Prisma 5.22; `.next` cleared afterward.\n- TypeScript: passed.\n- Lint: passed with the same 8 baseline warnings and no errors.\n- Unit: 70 suites, 803/803 passed. React `act(...)` warnings remain non-failing existing output.\n- Fresh migration: all 41 migrations applied.\n- Fresh integrity suite: 5/5 passed.\n- Guard proof: all 7 new constraints and both unique indexes were exercised; invalid writes failed and rollback/readback preserved the valid rows.\n- Populated migration: prior 40 migrations plus seed created 1,415 flights/10 airports; the refund migration applied without losing data.\n- Database: 30 suites, 186/186 passed.\n- Build: `npm run build` passed, including standalone sanitization.\n- Playwright: 40/40 passed serially in 5.6 minutes with clean teardown and no retry.\n\nEnvironment classification:\n\n- The first database run stopped only because my scratch database name did not end in `_test`; the repository safety guard correctly rejected it. Renaming that same scratch database produced the clean full result above. This was verifier setup, not a product regression.\n- Expected negative constraint diagnostics appeared during integrity tests.\n- No Playwright flake or `ECONNRESET` occurred.\n\nMutation audit:\n\n- 32 runs were reported.\n- Rows 1 and 17 are correctly excluded: row 1 attacked the wrong occurrence; row 17 was syntactically/semantically invalid and also touched unrelated code.\n- The remaining 30 mutants are credible first-attempt kills. The named assertions constrain exact provider amount/metadata, durable retry state and ordering, safe logging, action results, UI copy/focus/busy semantics, row snapshots, migration checks, and computed focus styling.\n- The strengthened terminal retry test genuinely persists `FAILED`, creates a distinct subsequent attempt, and verifies sequence order.\n- All source is restored. The selection gaps are the four findings above.\n\nSkipped with reachability justification:\n\n- Production dependency audit: package and lock files are unchanged.\n- Container secret scan/probes: Dockerfile, standalone output logic, and sanitizer are unchanged.\n\nFinal integrity:\n\n- Exactly 12 intended modified and 4 intended untracked paths; no staged or committed branch diff.\n- `git diff --check` clean.\n- HEAD equals `main` at `dab6bbf7cb63a49365daaa7e70508c458a5ab473`.\n- `.next` absent.\n- Port 3000 free.\n- No `travel_app_verify75_refund_%` or `travel_app_mutant%` scratch databases remain.\n- Database and Mailpit containers are healthy.\n- I changed no tracked source.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a007af-dc2d-7273-a829-7d59e29dc4f8"}}}
