d. Never a charge on its own. */\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:82: * the total was stored, and the amount charged is the one that may be refunded.\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:85: * more. The remainder is not refunded; refunding it would mean paying out more\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:97:        // dividing by zero. A zero-fare booking lands here and refunds zero.\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:112: * Why the refund came to what it did, in one line, for the history row.\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:115: * refund of zero next year has to be readable as \"cancelled inside the 24-hour\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:121:            return 'Cancelled after the airline disrupted the flight; refunded in full.';\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:123:            return `Cancelled within ${REFUND_CUTOFF_HOURS} hours of departure; no refund due.`;\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:125:            // On the fee, not on the refund: \"no fee\" and \"refunded in full\"\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:126:            // are different claims, and a booking that refunds nothing without\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:127:            // charging a fee would otherwise be recorded as refunded in full.\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:129:                ? 'Cancelled before the refund cut-off; no cancellation fee applied.'\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:130:                : `Cancelled before the refund cut-off; ${outcome.feeCents} minor units of the booking currency retained as the cancellation fee.`;\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:164:    // reach here, and apportioning by an empty list would silently refund\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:177:        // catalogue fare; reading it as zero here would refund nothing while\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:207:        return { allowed: false, reason: 'ALREADY_DEPARTED', refundCents: 0, feeCents: 0 };\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:215:            refundCents: booking.totalPriceCents,\nlib/cancellationPolicy.ts:223:        return { allowed: true, reason: 'INSIDE_CUTOFF', refundCents: 0, feeCents: 0 };\nlib/