{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T03:15:53.187Z","ordinal":21107,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a00891-92e2-7993-b673-a400a88d3204","author":"/root/verifier","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/verifier\nPayload:\nVerifier report for `feat/75-payment-receipts`\n\nFindings:\n\n1. Coverage gap: no durable test proves that a normal `PaymentAttempt` inserted directly as `CAPTURED` with `capturedAt: null` is stamped by the trigger. Existing tests cover capture through an update and a trigger-bypassed invalid insert. Removing `INSERT` from the trigger event would therefore escape the suite.\n\n2. Mutation-selection gap: the historical backfill was proven manually on the populated scratch database, but no automated test or reported mutant deletes the backfill statement. Such a change would remain green on CI’s fresh database and only fail against populated data.\n\nAll reported mutants themselves are valid. Rows 1–11 have direct, non-vacuous assertions:\n\n- CAPTURED-only selection, safe projection, authoritative receipt amount, receipt filtering, and all refund states are constrained directly.\n- The mobile grid mutant is constrained by exact receipt and document width assertions.\n- The capture date test distinguishes June 3 from June 1.\n- Trigger stamping, immutability, and the check constraint are exercised directly.\n- All 11 died on their reported first attempts and the final source is restored.\n\nExecutable results:\n\n- Prisma client generation: passed.\n- TypeScript: passed.\n- Lint: passed with the same 8 baseline warnings.\n- Unit: 70 suites, 812/812 passed.\n- Database: 31 suites, 201/201 passed.\n- Build: passed; sanitizer removed one `.env` file from standalone output.\n- Playwright: 40/40 passed in 5.9 minutes with clean teardown.\n- Fresh migration: all 42 migrations deployed; integrity suite 8/8 passed.\n- Populated migration: prior 41 migrations plus seed succeeded; a pre-existing CAPTURED attempt was backfilled from its exact `updatedAt`; trigger and constraint were installed once and application data remained intact.\n- Guard proof: update-to-CAPTURED stamped a timestamp, later writes could not move it, and a trigger-bypassed CAPTURED/null row was rejected.\n\nClassification:\n\n- Baseline unit increased from 808 to 812 with no regression.\n- Eight lint warnings match the supplied main baseline.\n- React `act(...)` warnings remained non-failing test noise.\n- Playwright emitted one non-failing `ECONNRESET/aborted` server message and one `Failed to load Stripe.js` browser message. No journey failed or was retried; this slice does not change either boundary. No clean-main Playwright baseline exists for stronger classification.\n- The previously reported malformed local development database was not reproduced and remains correctly classified as local database inconsistency.\n\nSkips:\n\n- Production dependency audit: package manifests and lockfile unchanged.\n- Container secret scan: Dockerfile, standalone sanitizer, and image path unchanged.\n\nIntegrity:\n\n- Exact intended status remains: 9 modified and 2 untracked files.\n- No staged or committed branch diff; `HEAD == main == bb599585`.\n- `git diff --check` clean.\n- `.next` removed.\n- Both verifier scratch databases dropped; no matching verifier or mutant databases remain.\n- Port 3000 is free.\n- PostgreSQL and Mailpit remain healthy.\n- No tracked source was changed by verification.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a007af-dc2d-7273-a829-7d59e29dc4f8"}}}
