{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T03:54:33.832Z","ordinal":21506,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a008b4-fbe8-7222-ba08-ea06a8f44415","author":"/root/verifier","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/verifier\nPayload:\nVerifier report: executable behavior is green, but two coverage-selection findings remain.\n\nFindings:\n\n1. Coverage gap — caller-supplied capture timestamps are not tested on the capture operation itself. A mutant changing the stamp to `COALESCE(NEW.\"capturedAt\", clock_timestamp())` would survive all 15 reported rows: direct CAPTURED tests supply null, while the pre-seed test has already had its false date cleared by the `ELSE` branch. The reviewed promise that capture ignores caller input therefore lacks durable coverage.\n\n2. Coverage gap — the CAPTURED-to-non-CAPTURED downgrade path is not directly tested. A mutant preserving the old timestamp only when `NEW.status = 'CAPTURED'` would pass the immutability test, clear the timestamp on downgrade, and allow the downgrade through the equivalence constraint. Row 15 proves the constraint rejects a mismatched row, but does not constrain this trigger interaction.\n\nCurrent behavior was independently proven correct: a forged timestamp supplied on CAPTURED insertion was replaced with current database time, and a CAPTURED-to-AUTHORIZED downgrade failed `PaymentAttempt_captured_has_time` and rolled back.\n\nResults:\n\n- Prisma generation: passed; `.next` cleared.\n- TypeScript: passed.\n- Lint: 0 errors, same 8 baseline warnings.\n- Unit: 70 suites, 812/812 passed.\n- Fresh migration: all 42 migrations deployed.\n- Fresh integrity suite: 12/12 passed.\n- Populated migration: passed. CAPTURED backfilled exactly from `updatedAt`; AUTHORIZED remained null; 1,415 flights and 10 airports remained; one trigger and constraint installed.\n- Full database: 31 suites, 205/205 passed.\n- Build: passed; sanitizer removed one standalone `.env`.\n- Full Playwright: 40/40 passed in 5.0 minutes with clean teardown.\n\nMutation audit:\n\n- Rows 1–13 remain valid and directly constrained.\n- Row 14 is valid: deleting `ELSE ... := NULL` makes the pre-seed test fail rather than returning null.\n- Row 15 is valid: weakening equivalence allows the trigger-bypassed AUTHORIZED/timestamp mismatch.\n- All 15 source mutants are restored, but rows 14–15 do not cover the two surgical interactions above.\n\nClassification:\n\n- No executable regression was observed.\n- Unit remains four tests above the 808-test main baseline.\n- React `act(...)`, expected constraint logs, and `NO_COLOR` warnings remain non-failing known noise.\n- Playwright emitted one non-failing `ECONNRESET/aborted` episode with duplicated uncaught-exception logging. No test failed or retried; this recurring noise is unrelated to the reviewed migration/test changes.\n\nSkips:\n\n- Dependency audit: package files unchanged.\n- Container scan: Dockerfile, standalone, and sanitizer paths unchanged.\n- UI re-review: no rendered production path changed after the prior successful review.\n\nIntegrity:\n\n- Exact intended status remains 9 modified plus 2 untracked files.\n- No staged or committed branch diff; `HEAD == main == bb599585`.\n- `git diff --check` clean.\n- `.next`, temporary Prisma copy, and both verifier databases removed.\n- No matching verifier or mutant scratch databases remain.\n- Port 3000 free; PostgreSQL and Mailpit healthy.\n- No tracked/status-reported file was changed by verification.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a007af-dc2d-7273-a829-7d59e29dc4f8"}}}
