{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T04:11:21.564Z","ordinal":21642,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a008c4-5c5b-7503-9ab8-4e52359ae7c8","author":"/root/verifier","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/verifier\nPayload:\nFinal verifier report: no actionable findings remain.\n\nResults:\n\n- Prisma generation: passed; `.next` cleared.\n- TypeScript: passed.\n- Lint: 0 errors, same 8 baseline warnings.\n- Unit: 70 suites, 812/812 passed.\n- Fresh migration: all 42 migrations deployed.\n- Fresh capture-time integrity: 13/13 passed.\n- Populated migration: passed:\n  - Historical CAPTURED timestamp exactly matched `updatedAt`.\n  - Historical AUTHORIZED timestamp remained null.\n  - Forged timestamp supplied during capture was replaced by database time.\n  - CAPTURED-to-AUTHORIZED downgrade was rejected and rolled back.\n  - 1,415 flights and 10 airports remained.\n  - Exactly one capture trigger and constraint were installed.\n- Full database: 31 suites, 206/206 passed.\n- Build: passed; sanitizer removed one standalone `.env`.\n- Full serial Playwright: 40/40 passed in 5.1 minutes with clean teardown.\n\nMutation audit:\n\n- Rows 1–15 remain valid and directly constrained.\n- Row 16 is directly killed by the forged direct-CAPTURED insert, which asserts a `Date` different from the supplied year-2000 value.\n- Row 17 is directly killed by the downgrade test, which requires the exact constraint rejection and rereads the durable original CAPTURED status/timestamp.\n- All 17 mutants are restored. The selection now covers receipt projection, customer-safe fields, responsive rendering, backfill, trigger insertion/update behavior, timestamp immutability, caller-input suppression, downgrade rejection, and both constraint directions.\n- No vacuous assertion or remaining changed-behavior gap found.\n\nClassification:\n\n- No regression or flake observed.\n- Unit remains four tests above the 808-test main baseline.\n- React `act(...)`, expected database-constraint logs, and `NO_COLOR` warnings remain known non-failing noise.\n- Playwright emitted one non-failing `ECONNRESET/aborted` message. No test failed or retried; this recurring server noise is unrelated to the final test-only fixes.\n\nSkips:\n\n- Dependency audit: package files unchanged.\n- Container scan: Dockerfile, standalone, and sanitizer paths unchanged.\n- UI re-review: final changes are database-invariant tests and cannot alter the previously reviewed rendered journey.\n\nIntegrity:\n\n- Exact intended status remains 9 modified plus 2 untracked files.\n- No staged or committed branch diff; `HEAD == main == bb599585`.\n- `git diff --check` clean.\n- `.next`, temporary Prisma copy, and both verifier databases removed.\n- No matching verifier or mutant scratch databases remain.\n- Port 3000 is free.\n- PostgreSQL and Mailpit remain healthy.\n- No tracked/status-reported file was changed by verification.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a007af-dc2d-7273-a829-7d59e29dc4f8"}}}
