{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T04:13:40.585Z","ordinal":21706,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_00fb20eee1c75140016a8138ee86d48198830c50f6b55093c0","status":"completed","call_id":"call_hELPkycX0HT256EugiZqe4Tg","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /tmp/travel-app-pr-75-receipts.md\\n+## Summary\\n+\\n+- add customer-safe payment receipts to the profile for captured bookings\\n+- show the captured amount, payment date, itinerary flight numbers, and durable refund outcome without exposing provider or idempotency identifiers\\n+- record an immutable database-owned `capturedAt`, backfill historical captured attempts, and reject forged timestamps or captured-state downgrades\\n+- keep receipt cards responsive and covered by the paid booking/refund journey\\n+\\n+## Why\\n+\\n+Issue #75 needs customers to see trustworthy payment history. Payment-attempt creation and later webhook timestamps are not the payment date, so this slice records the first durable capture time and uses that authoritative record for the receipt.\\n+\\n+## Validation\\n+\\n+- rendered UI review at 390x844, 768x1024, and 1440x900\\n+- `npx tsc --noEmit`\\n+- `npm run lint` (0 errors, 8 existing warnings)\\n+- `npm run test:unit` (812/812)\\n+- `npm run test:database` (206/206)\\n+- fresh and populated migration proofs, including backfill, forged-time rejection, and downgrade rollback\\n+- `npm run build`\\n+- `npx playwright test` (40/40)\\n+- 17 focused mutation checks audited and restored\\n+\\n+Advances #75. Broader operational reconciliation remains a follow-up slice.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a007af-dc2d-7273-a829-7d59e29dc4f8"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T04:13:40.956Z","ordinal":21707,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019ffe5b-1054-7c22-8afc-e97cb84c7b73","turn_id":"01a007af-dc2d-7273-a829-7d59e29dc4f8","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-6263667c-fb1c-4cdd-99d4-60b0ec6388cd","changes":{"/tmp/travel-app-pr-75-receipts.md":{"type":"add","content":"## Summary\n\n- add customer-safe payment receipts to the profile for captured bookings\n- show the captured amount, payment date, itinerary flight numbers, and durable refund outcome without exposing provider or idempotency identifiers\n- record an immutable database-owned `capturedAt`, backfill historical captured attempts, and reject forged timestamps or captured-state downgrades\n- keep receipt cards responsive and covered by the paid booking/refund journey\n\n## Why\n\nIssue #75 needs customers to see trustworthy payment history. Payment-attempt creation and later webhook timestamps are not the payment date, so this slice records the first durable capture time and uses that authoritative record for the receipt.\n\n## Validation\n\n- rendered UI review at 390x844, 768x1024, and 1440x900\n- `npx tsc --noEmit`\n- `npm run lint` (0 errors, 8 existing warnings)\n- `npm run test:unit` (812/812)\n- `npm run test:database` (206/206)\n- fresh and populated migration proofs, including backfill, forged-time rejection, and downgrade rollback\n- `npm run build`\n- `npx playwright test` (40/40)\n- 17 focused mutation checks audited and restored\n\nAdvances #75. Broader operational reconciliation remains a follow-up slice.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /tmp/travel-app-pr-75-receipts.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1786853620706,"completed_at_ms":1786853620956}}
