{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T04:14:06.789Z","ordinal":21723,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019ffe5b-1054-7c22-8afc-e97cb84c7b73","turn_id":"01a007af-dc2d-7273-a829-7d59e29dc4f8","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-52611c99-7b1f-4aae-acc8-c5e4527b924b","changes":{"/tmp/travel-app-pr-75-receipts.md":{"type":"delete","content":"## Summary\n\n- add customer-safe payment receipts to the profile for captured bookings\n- show the captured amount, payment date, itinerary flight numbers, and durable refund outcome without exposing provider or idempotency identifiers\n- record an immutable database-owned `capturedAt`, backfill historical captured attempts, and reject forged timestamps or captured-state downgrades\n- keep receipt cards responsive and covered by the paid booking/refund journey\n\n## Why\n\nIssue #75 needs customers to see trustworthy payment history. Payment-attempt creation and later webhook timestamps are not the payment date, so this slice records the first durable capture time and uses that authoritative record for the receipt.\n\n## Validation\n\n- rendered UI review at 390x844, 768x1024, and 1440x900\n- `npx tsc --noEmit`\n- `npm run lint` (0 errors, 8 existing warnings)\n- `npm run test:unit` (812/812)\n- `npm run test:database` (206/206)\n- fresh and populated migration proofs, including backfill, forged-time rejection, and downgrade rollback\n- `npm run build`\n- `npx playwright test` (40/40)\n- 17 focused mutation checks audited and restored\n\nAdvances #75. Broader operational reconciliation remains a follow-up slice.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nD /tmp/travel-app-pr-75-receipts.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1786853646456,"completed_at_ms":1786853646789}}
