{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T04:30:47.838Z","ordinal":21968,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019ffe5b-1054-7c22-8afc-e97cb84c7b73","turn_id":"01a008d3-a8d1-70b1-a975-44bf5aea121d","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_00fb20eee1c75140016a813cf629448198a03d5534f4c36fc5","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The existing design gives us a clean boundary: only provider-backed, nonterminal attempts older than the 10-minute checkout window will appear. That avoids touching an active customer checkout, and the operation will re-read Stripe’s current state rather than manufacture a webhook or retry a charge. I’m recording the required `main` baseline now, then I’ll branch and start with failing service/action/UI tests."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1786854646200,"completed_at_ms":1786854647838}}
