{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T04:36:53.847Z","ordinal":22099,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a008db-bdd7-7260-9f03-86efa573c597","call_id":"call_DEyClblkWQqSH6pXLUayhMv2","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 6.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"\n> travel-app@0.1.0 test:unit\n> npx jest --selectProjects unit --testPathPattern __tests__/app/actions.test.ts\n\nRunning one project: unit\nPASS unit __tests__/app/actions.test.ts\n  saveCityGuideAction authorization\n    ✓ rejects an unauthenticated user (151 ms)\n    ✓ rejects a non-admin user (3 ms)\n    ✓ rejects an admin whose staff factor has not been verified (4 ms)\n    ✓ allows an admin user and saves the guide (16 ms)\n    ✓ normalizes guide text before saving (4 ms)\n  deleteCityGuideAction authorization and execution\n    ✓ rejects an unauthenticated user (4 ms)\n    ✓ rejects a non-admin user (3 ms)\n    ✓ allows an admin user and deletes the guide (2 ms)\n  searchFlightsAction\n    ✓ filters flights by the selected origin and destination without date (67 ms)\n    ✓ queries by date without generating inventory (19 ms)\n    ✓ searches the inbound direction on its own route and date (17 ms)\n    ✓ keeps the outbound results when the return search fails (14 ms)\n    ✓ fails the whole search when the outbound fails (23 ms)\n    ✓ prices results at the cabin that was searched (7 ms)\n    ✓ marks flights the searched cabin does not operate, and keeps them (6 ms)\n    ✓ defaults to economy when no cabin is given (5 ms)\n    ✓ rejects a cabin it does not sell (3 ms)\n    ✓ reports no inbound for a one-way search (6 ms)\n    ✓ suggests the nearest operating dates when the exact date has no flights (18 ms)\n    ✓ excludes already-departed flights when searching today (18 ms)\n    ✓ rejects malformed and oversized searches before generation or database access (4 ms)\n    ✓ rejects invalid trip dates before generation or database access (3 ms)\n    ✓ rejects travel beyond the booking window before database access (3 ms)\n  getFlightRoutesAction\n    ✓ returns active routes with their next operating dates (3 ms)\n  bookFlightAction\n    ✓ refuses to create a booking until Stripe reports an authorized payment (7 ms)\n    ✓ calls FlightBookingService with flightId and userId from session and creates a notification (3 ms)\n    ✓ rejects oversized passenger arrays before calling the booking service (3 ms)\n    ✓ returns a recoverable seat error when checkout no longer owns its hold (3 ms)\n    ✓ maps a lost hold to the passenger and leg named by the claim (2 ms)\n    ✓ does not turn an unexpected booking failure into validation feedback (1 ms)\n    ✓ returns truthful retry feedback when booking succeeds before capture is confirmed (2 ms)\n    ✓ rejects bookings without passengers before calling the booking service (1 ms)\n    ✓ rejects client prices and payment identifiers before calling the booking service (1 ms)\n    ✓ does not duplicate booking notifications for an idempotent retry (1 ms)\n    ✓ creates the confirmation notification when a retry recovers payment capture (1 ms)\n  startCheckoutPaymentAction\n    ✓ starts a server-owned payment for the authenticated checkout (3 ms)\n    ✓ rejects card data and client prices before constructing a provider (1 ms)\n    ✓ rejects an unauthenticated caller before constructing a provider (1 ms)\n    ✓ returns recoverable field feedback when a payment checkout loses its hold (1 ms)\n  reconcilePaymentAttemptAction\n    ✓ lets verified staff refresh one payment attempt and revalidates the queue (1 ms)\n    ✓ rejects callers without verified staff access before constructing Stripe (2 ms)\n    ✓ rejects an invalid attempt ID before constructing Stripe (1 ms)\n    ✓ returns safe recoverable feedback when Stripe reconciliation fails (2 ms)\n  toggleFavoriteCityGuideAction\n    ✓ throws unauthorized if not logged in (1 ms)\n    ✓ removes favorite if it already exists (1 ms)\n    ✓ creates favorite if it does not exist (1 ms)\n    ✓ rejects malformed favorite identifiers before database access\n  submitCityGuideReviewAction\n    ✓ throws unauthorized if not logged in (1 ms)\n    ✓ creates a new review if logged in (1 ms)\n    ✓ rejects oversized review content before database access (1 ms)\n  cancelBookingAction\n    ✓ rejects an unauthenticated user (8 ms)\n    ✓ rejects a user trying to cancel another user's booking (2 ms)\n    ✓ allows a user to cancel their own booking (7 ms)\n    ✓ leaves the seat assignment alone, because the database releases it (2 ms)\n    ✓ records the refund the policy decided, on the transaction that cancels (4 ms)\n    ✓ durably submits the recorded refund for a captured booking (3 ms)\n    ✓ keeps a committed cancellation truthful when refund submission is unavailable (4 ms)\n    ✓ does not create a provider refund when the cancellation refunds zero (2 ms)\n    ✓ prices the cancellation from the read taken under the lock (3 ms)\n    ✓ refuses to cancel a booking whose flight has departed (3 ms)\n    ✓ allows an admin to cancel any booking (3 ms)\n  retryBookingRefundAction\n    ✓ lets the booking owner retry its durable refund (2 ms)\n    ✓ does not reveal another customer's refund (2 ms)\n    ✓ returns a stable validation result when the booking has no refund (2 ms)\n    ✓ maps provider failures to stable refund-safe copy (2 ms)\n  changeBookingSeatsAction\n    ✓ rejects an unauthenticated user (3 ms)\n    ✓ allows seat changes with valid inputs and transaction checks (7 ms)\n    ✓ rejects if a seat is already occupied (3 ms)\n    ✓ rejects a seat outside the passenger cabin layout (5 ms)\n    ✓ rejects seat changes after a booking is cancelled (3 ms)\n    ✓ rejects malformed seat changes before starting a transaction (3 ms)\n  deleteReviewAction\n    ✓ rejects an unauthenticated user (1 ms)\n    ✓ rejects a user trying to delete another user's review (2 ms)\n    ✓ allows a user to delete their own review (2 ms)\n    ✓ allows an admin to delete any review (2 ms)\n  admin flight schedule actions\n    saveFlightScheduleAction\n      ✓ rejects unauthenticated user (4 ms)\n      ✓ rejects non-admin user (2 ms)\n      ✓ rejects an explicitly empty seat pattern (8 ms)\n      ✓ refuses a place that is not an airport, before writing anything (5 ms)\n      ✓ reports both ends at once rather than one round trip each (3 ms)\n      ✓ allows admin to create a new flight schedule and generates flights (15 ms)\n      ✓ normalizes schedule identifiers before persistence (3 ms)\n      ✓ allows admin to update an existing flight schedule (13 ms)\n    deleteFlightScheduleAction\n      ✓ rejects unauthenticated user (3 ms)\n      ✓ allows admin to delete schedule (2 ms)\n    updateFlightStatusAction\n      ✓ rejects unauthenticated user (3 ms)\n      ✓ allows admin to update status and creates flight update notifications for affected users (7 ms)\n    user notifications actions\n      getUserNotificationsAction\n        ✓ returns empty array if unauthenticated (2 ms)\n        ✓ returns notifications for logged in user (2 ms)\n      markNotificationAsReadAction\n        ✓ rejects if unauthenticated (3 ms)\n        ✓ rejects if user does not own the notification (3 ms)\n        ✓ updates notification isRead to true if owned (3 ms)\n      markAllNotificationsAsReadAction\n        ✓ rejects if unauthenticated (3 ms)\n        ✓ marks all unread notifications as read for logged in user (2 ms)\n      generateFlightOccurrencesAction\n        ✓ rejects if unauthenticated (3 ms)\n        ✓ rejects if non-admin (3 ms)\n        ✓ generates flight instances and updates existing ones (11 ms)\n        ✓ rejects invalid seating configuration inputs (12 ms)\n        ✓ normalizes seat patterns before persisting occurrences (5 ms)\n        ✓ reports existing occurrences as updated (6 ms)\n        ✓ applies the requested layout after a concurrent occurrence create (6 ms)\n        ✓ rejects malformed or excessive occurrence date ranges (4 ms)\n        ✓ does not invalidate seats already assigned to passengers (7 ms)\n        ✓ does not move an occupied seat across cabin boundaries (5 ms)\n  getOccupiedSeatsAction authorization\n    ✓ refuses an unauthenticated caller, without reaching the database (2 ms)\n    ✓ refuses a session carrying no user id (2 ms)\n    ✓ answers any signed-in traveller, for any flight (3 ms)\n    ✓ still validates the flight id for a signed-in caller (11 ms)\n    ✓ answers who is asking before what they asked for (2 ms)\n  holdChosenSeatsAction input boundary\n    ✓ rejects a malformed checkout identifier before writing a hold (5 ms)\n    ✓ propagates an unexpected hold storage failure (2 ms)\n\nTest Suites: 1 passed, 1 total\nTests:       111 passed, 111 total\nSnapshots:   0 total\nTime:        3.47 s\nRan all test suites matching /__tests__\\/app\\/actions.test.ts/i.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a008d3-a8d1-70b1-a975-44bf5aea121d"}}}
