{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T05:22:05.222Z","ordinal":22905,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a00905-1d26-74b0-af90-bcc0f183c60c","author":"/root/verifier","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/verifier\nPayload:\nVerifier completed. Executable gates are green, with two actionable coverage findings.\n\nFindings:\n\n1. The new staff reconciliation lock/race contract is not constrained. `PaymentAttemptReconciliationService` acquires the shared PaymentIntent lock and rereads the binding at [lib/paymentWebhookService.ts:91](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/lib/paymentWebhookService.ts:91), but its four tests are sequential. Existing concurrency coverage exercises `PaymentWebhookService`, not the new staff service. Deleting the staff lock or binding reread would leave the suite green.\n\n2. The recovery-queue selection contract is only partially constrained:\n\n   - The “fifty oldest” test asserts only length, not which IDs or order, so removing/reversing `ORDER BY` would survive.\n   - The ten-minute rule uses fixtures at now and eleven minutes; changing the threshold from ten to nine minutes would survive.\n   - Eligible states cover only `REQUIRES_ACTION` and `PROCESSING`. `CREATING`, `REQUIRES_PAYMENT_METHOD`, `REQUIRES_CONFIRMATION`, and `AUTHORIZED` could be wrongly excluded without detection.\n\nGate results:\n\n- `npx tsc --noEmit`: passed.\n- `npm run lint`: passed, 0 errors and the same 8 baseline warnings.\n- `npm run test:unit`: 72 suites, 821/821 passed. Existing unrelated React `act(...)` warnings appeared in `TravelGuideClient` and `ProfileClient`.\n- `npm run test:database`: permitted rerun passed, 32 suites and 212/212 tests. The initial sandboxed run failed uniformly because localhost Postgres was inaccessible; this was environmental.\n- `npm run build`: passed outside the process sandbox, including standalone sanitization. Initial sandbox run failed when Turbopack was denied an internal port bind; environmental.\n- `npx playwright test`: 41/41 passed serially in 5.4 minutes with clean teardown. One non-failing `ECONNRESET / Error: aborted` server message appeared during the admin journey; no assertion failed and it did not recur as a test failure.\n\nMutant audit:\n\n- All 23 reported edits are restored.\n- Each named test contains a direct assertion constraining its reported mutant.\n- Rows 1–4 constrain provider/terminal/staleness/limit filtering; rows 5–11 constrain durable reconciliation, bindings, transitions, and provider identity; rows 12–17 constrain staff authorization, validation ordering, revalidation, safe logging/result serialization; rows 18–21 constrain focus, busy/disabled semantics, and timestamp refresh; row 22 constrains the server/client ISO boundary; row 23 constrains the exact focus outline.\n- Selection remains incomplete due to the two findings above.\n\nSkips:\n\n- Migration proof: not reachable; no schema or migration change.\n- Production dependency audit: not reachable; package files unchanged.\n- Container secret scan/probes: not reachable; Dockerfile, standalone, and sanitizer paths unchanged.\n\nIntegrity:\n\n- Git status remains exactly the intended 6 modified and 7 untracked paths; no staged or committed diff.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Port 3000 is free after Playwright teardown.\n- No scratch database was created. Existing DB/Mailpit services remain running.\n- `.next` exists only as ignored build output.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a008d3-a8d1-70b1-a975-44bf5aea121d"}}}
