{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T05:29:25.291Z","ordinal":23077,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a0090b-d42b-7cb2-b80c-401bac070b96","call_id":"call_vk1oxZCFPGf5W0sRoUaoP6NY","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/ui_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Throwaway Playwright fallback used because browser-plugin tooling was unavailable.\\n\\nNo actionable findings.\\n\\nPassed at 390×844, 768×1024, and 1440×900:\\n\\n- Verified-staff MFA sign-in, keyboard activation of `/admin` → Payment Recovery, and keyboard activation of each refresh control.\\n- Exact explanatory copy and truthful stale-card details.\\n- Provider-intent and checkout references wrapped with computed `overflow-wrap: anywhere`; cards and documents had no horizontal overflow.\\n- Delayed real action exposed exact `Refreshing payment status…`, disabled state, and `aria-busy=\\\"true\\\"`.\\n- Unchanged result showed exact `Payment status is still REQUIRES_PAYMENT_METHOD.`\\n- Safe failure showed exact `Payment status could not be refreshed. Try again later.`\\n- Both feedback states owned focus after settling and had computed 3px solid amber `rgb(251, 191, 36)` outline, 3px offset, and halo.\\n- Desktop changed-state coverage rendered exact `Payment status refreshed from PROCESSING to CAPTURED.`, updated the target card to `CAPTURED`, and disabled its `Payment reconciled` control.\\n- No reconciliation created a webhook event.\\n- No browser console/page errors, warnings, request failures, or HTTP 500s occurred in the relevant admin journeys. The induced provider-missing error produced only the expected sanitized server log with the local attempt ID.\\n- A phone setup run initially recorded `POST /admin net::ERR_ABORTED` when navigation intentionally abandoned a header notification action; this was a harness-listener issue, excluded before the remaining bounded run.\\n\\nScreenshots:\\n\\n- Phone: [stale](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-payment-recovery-phone-390x844-stale.png), [pending](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-payment-recovery-phone-390x844-pending.png), [unchanged](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-payment-recovery-phone-390x844-unchanged-success.png), [safe error](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-payment-recovery-phone-390x844-safe-error.png)\\n- Tablet: [stale](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-payment-recovery-tablet-768x1024-stale.png), [pending](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/REDACTED.png), [unchanged](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-payment-recovery-tablet-768x1024-unchanged-success.png), [safe error](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-payment-recovery-tablet-768x1024-safe-error.png)\\n- Desktop: [stale](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-payment-recovery-desktop-1440x900-stale.png), [pending](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-payment-recovery-desktop-1440x900-pending.png), [unchanged](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-payment-recovery-desktop-1440x900-unchanged-success.png), [safe error](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-payment-recovery-desktop-1440x900-safe-error.png), [changed terminal](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue75-payment-recovery-desktop-1440x900-changed-terminal.png)\\n\\nCleanup/integrity: created users, bookings, attempts, webhook events, notifications, and holds are all zero; port 3000 is free. Git remains exactly six intended modified tracked files plus seven intended untracked paths, with no staged or committed diff.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/verifier\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Verifier completed. Executable gates are green, with two actionable coverage findings.\\n\\nFindings:\\n\\n1. The new staff reconciliation lock/race contract is not constrained. `PaymentAttemptReconciliationService` acquires the shared PaymentIntent lock and rereads the binding at [lib/paymentWebhookService.ts:91](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/lib/paymentWebhookService.ts:91), but its four tests are sequential. Existing concurrency coverage exercises `PaymentWebhookService`, not the new staff service. Deleting the staff lock or binding reread would leave the suite green.\\n\\n2. The recovery-queue selection contract is only partially constrained:\\n\\n   - The “fifty oldest” test asserts only length, not which IDs or order, so removing/reversing `ORDER BY` would survive.\\n   - The ten-minute rule uses fixtures at now and eleven minutes; changing the threshold from ten to nine minutes would survive.\\n   - Eligible states cover only `REQUIRES_ACTION` and `PROCESSING`. `CREATING`, `REQUIRES_PAYMENT_METHOD`, `REQUIRES_CONFIRMATION`, and `AUTHORIZED` could be wrongly excluded without detection.\\n\\nGate results:\\n\\n- `npx tsc --noEmit`: passed.\\n- `npm run lint`: passed, 0 errors and the same 8 baseline warnings.\\n- `npm run test:unit`: 72 suites, 821/821 passed. Existing unrelated React `act(...)` warnings appeared in `TravelGuideClient` and `ProfileClient`.\\n- `npm run test:database`: permitted rerun passed, 32 suites and 212/212 tests. The initial sandboxed run failed uniformly because localhost Postgres was inaccessible; this was environmental.\\n- `npm run build`: passed outside the process sandbox, including standalone sanitization. Initial sandbox run failed when Turbopack was denied an internal port bind; environmental.\\n- `npx playwright test`: 41/41 passed serially in 5.4 minutes with clean teardown. One non-failing `ECONNRESET / Error: aborted` server message appeared during the admin journey; no assertion failed and it did not recur as a test failure.\\n\\nMutant audit:\\n\\n- All 23 reported edits are restored.\\n- Each named test contains a direct assertion constraining its reported mutant.\\n- Rows 1–4 constrain provider/terminal/staleness/limit filtering; rows 5–11 constrain durable reconciliation, bindings, transitions, and provider identity; rows 12–17 constrain staff authorization, validation ordering, revalidation, safe logging/result serialization; rows 18–21 constrain focus, busy/disabled semantics, and timestamp refresh; row 22 constrains the server/client ISO boundary; row 23 constrains the exact focus outline.\\n- Selection remains incomplete due to the two findings above.\\n\\nSkips:\\n\\n- Migration proof: not reachable; no schema or migration change.\\n- Production dependency audit: not reachable; package files unchanged.\\n- Container secret scan/probes: not reachable; Dockerfile, standalone, and sanitizer paths unchanged.\\n\\nIntegrity:\\n\\n- Git status remains exactly the intended 6 modified and 7 untracked paths; no staged or committed diff.\\n- `git diff --check` passed.\\n- Port 3000 is free after Playwright teardown.\\n- No scratch database was created. Existing DB/Mailpit services remain running.\\n- `.next` exists only as ignored build output.\\n\\n\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a008d3-a8d1-70b1-a975-44bf5aea121d"}}}
