{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T05:39:46.566Z","ordinal":23169,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a00915-4f05-7e43-8b9d-d8118809f31e","author":"/root/verifier","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/verifier\nPayload:\nFinal verifier re-hand completed. Both prior coverage gaps are closed; no new regression or coverage gap found.\n\nFindings:\n\n- Unrelated Playwright flake: the full suite finished 40/41 because unchanged `e2e/travelguide.spec.ts` recorded one transient resource 404 at its final console-error assertion. The exact test then passed 1/1 in isolation. The changed payment-recovery journey passed. With no clean-main Playwright baseline, I classify this as an unrelated flake—not a confirmed pre-existing baseline failure and not caused by the test-only re-hand.\n- One non-failing `ECONNRESET / Error: aborted` server message appeared during the booking expiry journey; that journey passed.\n\nChecks:\n\n- `npx tsc --noEmit`: passed.\n- `npm run lint`: passed with 0 errors and the same 8 baseline warnings.\n- `npm run test:unit`: 72 suites, 821/821 passed. Existing unrelated React `act(...)` warnings remained in Travel Guide and Profile tests.\n- `npm run test:database`: 32 suites, 215/215 passed.\n- `npm run build`: passed, including standalone environment sanitization.\n- `npx playwright test`: 40 passed, 1 flaky failure described above.\n- Isolated `npx playwright test e2e/travelguide.spec.ts`: 1/1 passed.\n\nMutant audit:\n\n- All 29 reported mutants are restored and auditable.\n- Original rows 1–23 remain directly constrained.\n- Row 24 is constrained by both the staff concurrency call-count/final-status proof and advisory-wait binding-race proof.\n- Row 25 is constrained by the exact post-lock binding error and provider-not-called assertion.\n- Rows 26 and 29 are constrained by the exact ordered 50-ID sequence.\n- Row 27 is constrained by explicit 10-minute-qualified and 9-minute-excluded fixtures.\n- Row 28 is constrained by exact-set coverage of all six nonterminal statuses.\n- The earlier lock/reread and queue ordering/cutoff/status findings are fully closed.\n\nSkips:\n\n- Migration proof: no schema or migration change.\n- Production dependency audit: package files unchanged.\n- Container image scan/probes: Dockerfile, standalone, and sanitizer sources unchanged.\n- UI re-review: the re-hand changed database tests only; prior rendered review remains applicable.\n\nIntegrity:\n\n- Git status remains exactly the intended 6 modified and 7 untracked paths.\n- No staged or committed branch diff.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Port 3000 is free after both Playwright teardowns.\n- No scratch database was created.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a008d3-a8d1-70b1-a975-44bf5aea121d"}}}
