{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T17:52:05.841Z","ordinal":23550,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019ffe5b-1054-7c22-8afc-e97cb84c7b73","turn_id":"01a00bb2-2acf-7d53-ab0c-ded966187af9","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_00fb20eee1c75140016a81f8c1c2708198abe13e46a307d529","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Next should be [#234 — Rebook a disrupted itinerary](https://github.com/scottdensmore/travel-app/issues/234), completing the remaining work under [#76 / P2.4](https://github.com/scottdensmore/travel-app/issues/76) before starting #77 check-in.\n\nI recommend beginning with a short plan/prototype to settle the key domain choice:\n\n- Preserve the original booking and payment history.\n- Create a linked replacement booking rather than rewriting the original itinerary.\n- Define seat release/reselection and fare-difference behavior.\n- Exclude account credit initially; it needs a separate balance model.\n\nThen we can choose the smallest complete rebooking journey for the first PR. The repository is clean on synchronized `main`, with no open PRs.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":595,"lineEnd":625,"note":"roadmap ordering and repository triage workflow"}],"rolloutIds":["019f5d63-d808-77f2-8f4c-7d1415c91a7c"]}},"started_at_ms":1786902721807,"completed_at_ms":1786902725841}}
