{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T17:56:29.365Z","ordinal":23614,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019ffe5b-1054-7c22-8afc-e97cb84c7b73","turn_id":"01a00bb5-84d2-75b2-a295-9f36c2da7b8e","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_00fb20eee1c75140016a81f9cb3ce481988dc6015bdb8fae4c","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The executable model rejects both tempting shortcuts: mutating legs loses itinerary/seat history, while a new booking loses the stable reference and splits passenger/payment ownership. Versioning the itinerary under the same booking is the only option that preserves all eight current invariants. I’m checking its integration cost now—especially how many readers need an “active legs only” rule and whether existing refund/payment records can represent fare differences cleanly."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1786902987287,"completed_at_ms":1786902989365}}
