{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T17:57:10.255Z","ordinal":23628,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019ffe5b-1054-7c22-8afc-e97cb84c7b73","turn_id":"01a00bb5-84d2-75b2-a295-9f36c2da7b8e","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_00fb20eee1c75140016a81f9f3e14c8198a42a73ec084ac64c","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The payment integration changes the product choice: existing refunds are deliberately cancellation-only, and a booking currently owns one captured PaymentIntent. Rather than inventing a second charge/refund ledger for an airline-caused disruption, the cleaner policy is to waive fare differences for a same-route, same-cabin replacement. The customer either takes the original full refund or rebooks at no additional charge; the catalog difference is recorded for audit but no money moves. I’m testing that policy across cheaper, equal, and more-expensive replacements now."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1786903027925,"completed_at_ms":1786903030255}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T17:57:10.258Z","ordinal":23629,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_00fb20eee1c75140016a81f9f3e14c8198a42a73ec084ac64c","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The payment integration changes the product choice: existing refunds are deliberately cancellation-only, and a booking currently owns one captured PaymentIntent. Rather than inventing a second charge/refund ledger for an airline-caused disruption, the cleaner policy is to waive fare differences for a same-route, same-cabin replacement. The customer either takes the original full refund or rebooks at no additional charge; the catalog difference is recorded for audit but no money moves. I’m testing that policy across cheaper, equal, and more-expensive replacements now."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a00bb5-84d2-75b2-a295-9f36c2da7b8e"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T17:57:15.818Z","ordinal":23630,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_00fb20eee1c75140016a81f9f635688198bd3209c98794b2be","status":"completed","call_id":"call_ijZQCluR2TfaEwISRuwZmT4N","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /tmp/rebooking-model-prototype.mjs\\n@@\\n function addVersionedItinerary(replacementFareCents = replacement.fareCents) {\\n     const differenceCents = replacementFareCents - original.capturedCents;\\n@@\\n         adjustments: [{\\n@@\\n         }],\\n     };\\n }\\n+\\n+function waiveDisruptionFareDifference(replacementFareCents) {\\n+    const rebooked = addVersionedItinerary(replacementFareCents);\\n+    const catalogDifferenceCents = replacementFareCents - original.capturedCents;\\n+    return {\\n+        ...rebooked,\\n+        adjustments: [{\\n+            kind: 'NONE',\\n+            amountCents: 0,\\n+            status: 'NOT_REQUIRED',\\n+            catalogDifferenceCents,\\n+            waivedDifferenceCents: Math.max(catalogDifferenceCents, 0),\\n+        }],\\n+    };\\n+}\\n@@\\n for (const [fareCents, expected] of [\\n@@\\n     );\\n }\\n+\\n+for (const fareCents of [24_000, 30_000, 35_500]) {\\n+    const waived = waiveDisruptionFareDifference(fareCents);\\n+    assert.equal(waived.adjustments[0].kind, 'NONE');\\n+    assert.equal(waived.adjustments[0].amountCents, 0);\\n+    assert.equal(waived.paymentIntentIds.length, 1);\\n+    assert.equal(waived.paymentIntentIds[0], 'pi_original');\\n+    assert.deepEqual(Object.values(invariantResults(waived)), Array(8).fill(true));\\n+}\\n@@\\n console.log('Fare adjustment cases: equal=NONE, cheaper=REFUND, dearer=CHARGE.');\\n+console.log('Disruption waiver cases: cheaper/equal/dearer all keep the original capture and move no money.');\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a00bb5-84d2-75b2-a295-9f36c2da7b8e"}}}
