{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T18:12:47.900Z","ordinal":24021,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019ffe5b-1054-7c22-8afc-e97cb84c7b73","turn_id":"01a00bba-29dd-7100-8715-811d18e7c7e1","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_00fb20eee1c75140016a81fd9e336c81988c2e0ceab6d46024","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The new “event must name at least one replaced leg” test exposed a real hole: a transaction can commit a `BookingRebooking` with zero mappings. The SQL defines the deferred trigger, so I’m checking the installed trigger and PostgreSQL timing semantics now; I’ll fix the database contract, not weaken the test."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1786903966255,"completed_at_ms":1786903967900}}
