{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T18:58:59.768Z","ordinal":25202,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a00bf1-0437-7790-b80e-c695c1d8844d","author":"/root/ui_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/ui_review\nPayload:\nBrowser plugin tools were absent; I used the mandated throwaway Playwright fallback.\n\nActionable finding:\n\n- Blocking — deleting a rebooked parent with `prisma.booking.deleteMany({ where: { id } })` fails with `BookingRebookingLeg_fromLegId_fkey`. The migration’s immediate `NO ACTION` leg references at [migration.sql](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/prisma/migrations/20260816181000_version_itinerary_legs/migration.sql:90) contradict its promised whole-booking cascade at [migration.sql](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/prisma/migrations/20260816181000_version_itinerary_legs/migration.sql:293). The valid review fixture could only be cleaned by disabling triggers locally in the disposable database and deleting exact rows in dependency order. Add coverage for the `deleteMany({ id })`/bulk-cleanup path; existing `.delete()` coverage does not catch this query-shape failure.\n\nRendered UI otherwise passed:\n\n- `/profile` at 390×844, 768×1024, and 1440×900 showed replacement `UI234-NEW-013d7` exactly once, route Seattle → San Francisco and seat 14C. The superseded Detroit flight and seat 11A never rendered.\n- No horizontal document overflow at any customer width.\n- Keyboard Tab reached Change Seats with a visible focus ring.\n- Admin Recent Bookings showed only the replacement.\n- Replacement manifest showed one confirmed Ada Rebooking, seat 14C; original occurrence showed zero bookings/passengers.\n- Manifest opened by keyboard, focused its close control, trapped focus, and returned focus to the trigger on Escape.\n- No console warnings/errors, page errors, failed requests, or HTTP 500 responses.\n\nScreenshots: [phone](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue234-profile-phone-390x844.png), [tablet](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue234-profile-tablet-768x1024.png), [desktop](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue234-profile-desktop-1440x900.png), [admin dashboard](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue234-admin-dashboard-desktop-1440x900.png), [replacement manifest](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue234-admin-replacement-manifest-desktop-1440x900.png), [original empty manifest](/home/scottdensmore/Developer/scottdensmore/travel-app/test-results/ui-review/issue234-admin-original-empty-manifest-desktop-1440x900.png).\n\nIntegrity: all scratch fixture tables are clean, port 3000 is free, no staged or committed branch diff appeared, and Git remains exactly 11 intended modified files plus 3 intended untracked paths.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a00bba-29dd-7100-8715-811d18e7c7e1"}}}
