{"timestamp":"2026-08-16T19:15:40.276Z","ordinal":25492,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019ffe5b-1054-7c22-8afc-e97cb84c7b73","turn_id":"01a00bba-29dd-7100-8715-811d18e7c7e1","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_00fb20eee1c75140016a820c5a40348198879b1ee8aa5c6575","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The verifier found a real append-only bypass: within one transaction, a caller can delete and reinsert the audit event/mapping with altered history, because the deferred guard currently checks only that a replacement mapping exists at commit. The fix is bounded: make any mapping deletion fail whenever its historical source leg still exists, regardless of whether a look-alike mapping was reinserted; whole-booking deletion still passes because the source leg is gone by commit. I’ll wait for the verifier’s remaining gates, then add delete-and-reinsert regressions and mutate that exact condition."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1786907738311,"completed_at_ms":1786907740276}}
